.TH PRINTF "MARCH 22 2026" "VERSION 1.0" "PRINTF"

.SH NAME
printf - custom printf function formatted for output conversion

.SH REQUIREMENTS TO USE
#include "main.h"
int _printf(const char *format, ...);
A README.md file, at the root of the folder of the project
Code should use the Betty style. It will be checked using betty-style.pl and betty-doc.pl
No global variables allowed

.SH DESCRIPTION
This function acts as a basic printf standard function.

It prints out standard output by using write().

The format string handles text and conversion specifers:

.TP
%c - characters
%s - strings
%d and %i - integers
%% - prints a percent sign

.SH
The return value is the number of characters printed by the function, excluding the terminating null byte.

.SH EXAMPLES
_printf("hello %s\n", "world", 1, 2, 3, 4);
.br
Output: hello world

_printf("Did you know: %s just fixed a truck using %d bolts and pure determination %c\n", "Josh", 4, '!');
.br
Output: Did you know: Josh just fixed a truck using 4 bolts and pure determination !

.SH LIMITATIONS
If an unknown conversion specifier is used, eg %r, it will simply print %r as the code has not been designed to handle these conversion specifiers.